# Mission: Forensic truth audit ZCoder v1.40.0, repair all Anthropic inaccuracies, then discover and implement the next legitimate upgrade

You are working directly inside the current ZCoder repository after the v1.40.0 release-gate work.

Treat **all previous release reports, audit documents, tests, model tables, comments, and implementation claims as potentially wrong until independently verified against current first-party Anthropic documentation**.

This is not merely another feature-addition pass.

Your priorities are:

1. prove that v1.40.0 is factually correct;
2. fix any false-positive release-gate results;
3. fix runtime behavior affected by those inaccuracies;
4. strengthen tests so the same class of error cannot recur;
5. then discover all newer or still-missing Anthropic capabilities;
6. implement legitimate production-useful gaps;
7. determine whether the resulting release should be v1.40.1, v1.41.0, or another SemVer version.

---

# 0. Non-negotiable source policy

Use **first-party sources only** for Anthropic platform facts.

Authoritative sources include:

* Claude Platform release notes
* Claude API reference
* Models overview
* Pricing
* Model deprecations
* Model migration guides
* Managed Agents documentation
* Agent SDK documentation
* Claude Code official changelog
* Admin API
* Compliance API
* Agent Skills
* MCP
* Claude Platform on AWS
* Amazon Bedrock Anthropic documentation where appropriate
* Google Cloud Anthropic documentation where appropriate
* Microsoft Foundry Anthropic documentation where appropriate
* Anthropic Help Center for Enterprise functionality
* Anthropic official announcements when they define product/API behavior

Do NOT use:

* blog reposts
* SEO pages
* Reddit
* Stack Overflow
* copied documentation
* generated summaries
* prior ZCoder documentation as source-of-truth
* assumptions from API naming

For every fact that affects code, capture its authoritative URL or source document in the audit report.

---

# 1. Establish baseline

Before changing anything:

```bash
git status --short
git log -20 --oneline
git tag --sort=-version:refname | head -20

python --version
python -m pytest -q
python main.py --help
git diff --check
```

Also run available quality checks:

```bash
ruff check .
black --check .
mypy .
```

Record baseline results.

Do not hide failures.

---

# 2. Re-open and challenge the v1.40.0 gate report

Find the release-gate document that claims approximately:

* v1.40.0
* zero P0/P1 blockers
* ~530 tests passing
* complete Anthropic coverage

Treat the PASS verdict as an assertion to test, not a fact.

Create:

```text
docs/v1.40.0-truth-audit.md
```

or the repository's correct equivalent.

For every row of the previous gate report, independently assign:

```text
VERIFIED_TRUE
FACTUALLY_WRONG
PARTIALLY_TRUE
IMPLEMENTATION_WRONG
TEST_FALSE_POSITIVE
STALE
UNVERIFIABLE
DOCS_ONLY
```

Include source evidence.

