---

# 22. Release-gate generator

Improve release auditing so future gates cannot declare PASS merely because tests pass.

A PASS requires:

```text
CODE_PASS
TEST_PASS
DOC_PASS
SOURCE_TRUTH_PASS
MODEL_MATRIX_PASS
PRICING_PASS
DEPRECATION_PASS
WIRE_FORMAT_PASS
CLI_WIRING_PASS
```

Generate machine-readable:

```json
{
  "result": "PASS",
  "source_truth_verified": true,
  "latest_release_note_date": "...",
  "p0": 0,
  "p1": 0,
  "false_positive_claims": 0
}
```

If any previous audit claim is factually wrong:

```text
SOURCE_TRUTH_PASS = false
```

until corrected.

---

# 23. Version decision

Do not assume v1.41.0.

Choose after seeing the actual changes.

Use:

### v1.40.1

If work is primarily:

* factual corrections
* pricing corrections
* header/metadata correctness
* regression fixes
* docs corrections

### v1.41.0

If significant backward-compatible functionality is also added.

### major release

Only for intentional incompatible changes.

Document the SemVer decision.

---

# 24. Required implementation workflow

Follow exactly:

## Phase A — Baseline

Run tests and capture repository state.

## Phase B — Truth audit

Re-fetch official Anthropic sources.

## Phase C — Find contradictions

Compare every v1.40 gate claim.

## Phase D — P0/P1 repairs

Correct factual/runtime defects immediately.

## Phase E — Regression protection

Add independent conformance tests.

## Phase F — New-feature discovery

Diff current Anthropic documentation against implementation.

## Phase G — Implement

Implement every applicable, public, production-useful P0/P1 gap.

Implement sensible P2 gaps where low-risk.

## Phase H — Documentation

Update all affected documentation.

## Phase I — Full verification

Run complete suite.

## Phase J — Adversarial second pass

Search again specifically for anything you incorrectly marked complete.

